WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.095
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.395 --> 00:00:08.851
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:17.434
Unit seven: Part 3: Graphics and Speaker Intention. Today you will combine what you hear with a chart and understand what speakers mean.

4
00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:20.270
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:24.768
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:26.548
Graphic.

7
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.699
Graphic means a chart, map, table or list.

8
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:32.691
Look at the graphic.

9
00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:35.936
Your turn. Say: Graphic.

10
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:39.789
Graphic.

11
00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:41.447
Schedule.

12
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.600
Schedule means a plan of times.

13
00:00:45.217 --> 00:00:46.438
Check the schedule.

14
00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.911
Your turn. Say: Schedule.

15
00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:53.849
Schedule.

16
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:55.619
Price list.

17
00:00:56.617 --> 00:00:58.779
Price list means a list of costs.

18
00:00:59.383 --> 00:01:01.174
The price list is on the screen.

19
00:01:01.783 --> 00:01:04.563
Your turn. Say: Price list.

20
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.587
Price list.

21
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:10.386
Intend.

22
00:01:11.383 --> 00:01:13.186
Intend means to plan to do.

23
00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:15.423
She intends to cancel.

24
00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:18.657
Your turn. Say: Intend.

25
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.443
Intend.

26
00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:24.173
Imply.

27
00:01:25.183 --> 00:01:27.961
Imply means to suggest without saying directly.

28
00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:30.341
He implies he is too busy.

29
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.138
Your turn. Say: Imply.

30
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.152
Imply.

31
00:01:37.917 --> 00:01:39.127
Sarcastic.

32
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:43.684
Sarcastic means saying the opposite to be funny or critical.

33
00:01:44.283 --> 00:01:45.853
That sounds sarcastic.

34
00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.975
Your turn. Say: Sarcastic.

35
00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:52.985
Sarcastic.

36
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:54.380
Quote.

37
00:01:55.383 --> 00:01:57.290
Quote means a price for a job.

38
00:01:57.883 --> 00:01:59.059
Send me a quote.

39
00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:02.430
Your turn. Say: Quote.

40
00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:05.943
Quote.

41
00:02:06.683 --> 00:02:07.557
Match.

42
00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:11.281
Match means to connect two pieces of information.

43
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:13.709
Match the speaker with the room.

44
00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:16.632
Your turn. Say: Match.

45
00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:20.723
Match.

46
00:02:21.533 --> 00:02:25.033
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.883 --> 00:02:28.974
Visal, what is different in graphic questions?

48
00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:38.703
One of the three questions uses a table, map or list. You must combine what you hear with the information printed in the graphic.

49
00:02:39.817 --> 00:02:41.027
How do I answer them?

50
00:02:42.117 --> 00:02:54.579
Study the graphic first, and notice what is missing, such as a room number. Then listen for the detail that fills the gap, for example a time, a price or a name.

51
00:02:55.683 --> 00:02:57.834
What are speaker intention questions?

52
00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:09.694
They quote a line, such as I wouldn't say that, and ask what the speaker means. Listen to the whole context, because the surface words may not give the real meaning.

53
00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:12.310
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:17.042
Grammar focus: Strategy: graphic plus audio.

55
00:03:17.342 --> 00:03:18.506
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.217 --> 00:03:22.726
The graphic shows room numbers, and the speaker says the time.

57
00:03:23.617 --> 00:03:26.557
I wouldn't say that can mean the speaker disagrees politely.

58
00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:34.878
Look at the graphic before the audio. Listen for the detail that fills the gap, and use the whole conversation to understand a quoted line.

59
00:03:35.617 --> 00:03:38.977
Be careful! Don't say: I ignore the graphic.

60
00:03:40.933 --> 00:03:43.688
Say: I combine the graphic with the audio.

61
00:03:43.988 --> 00:03:45.267
Use the graphic.

62
00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:48.417
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:49.233 --> 00:03:50.467
Using a Schedule.

64
00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:54.368
A manager and an assistant look at a meeting schedule on a screen.

65
00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:58.632
The room numbers are printed, but the times are missing.

66
00:03:59.633 --> 00:04:02.457
The assistant says the sales meeting starts at ten.

67
00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:06.349
The manager says, I wouldn't say that meeting is urgent.

68
00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:09.588
The assistant understands that it can wait.

69
00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:14.899
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.471
A graphic can be a blank.

71
00:04:17.771 --> 00:04:20.948
A, joke. B, table. C, poem.

72
00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.244
The answer is B: table.

73
00:04:27.383 --> 00:04:29.093
What is missing from the schedule?

74
00:04:29.393 --> 00:04:32.988
A, rooms. B, names. C, times.

75
00:04:36.533 --> 00:04:38.324
The answer is C: times.

76
00:04:39.483 --> 00:04:41.413
When does the sales meeting start?

77
00:04:41.713 --> 00:04:45.274
A, at ten. B, at noon. C, at nine.

78
00:04:48.833 --> 00:04:50.577
The answer is A: at ten.

79
00:04:51.717 --> 00:04:54.285
'I wouldn't say that meeting is urgent' means blank.

80
00:04:54.585 --> 00:04:58.924
A, it is cancelled. B, it can wait. C, it is urgent.

81
00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:04.141
The answer is B: it can wait.

82
00:05:05.283 --> 00:05:07.294
You should look at the graphic blank.

83
00:05:07.594 --> 00:05:12.304
A, after the test. B, never. C, before the audio.

84
00:05:15.867 --> 00:05:18.482
The answer is C: before the audio.

85
00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:22.702
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.235
How do you answer a question that uses a graphic?

87
00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.748
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:37.048 --> 00:05:51.591
I study the graphic before the audio starts and notice which information is missing. Then I listen for the detail that fills the gap. For a quoted line, I use the whole conversation to understand what the speaker really means.

89
00:05:51.891 --> 00:05:53.914
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:54.817 --> 00:06:00.209
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: graphic plus audio.

91
00:06:00.509 --> 00:06:04.926
Today's value is analytical thinking. Look for the pattern underneath the surface.

92
00:06:05.226 --> 00:06:07.727
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

93
00:06:08.027 --> 00:06:10.738
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

